    freestanding_match_over_fserror_yields_default_2026-09-01, 0, "2026-11-28 p3sweep5: the doc's addenda audited history but missed the transplant fix. Verified: interpreter D1=6 D2=true D3=6 D4=2 D5=1042 D6=2007 (matches doc); hosted AOT cranelift green (self-contained, std-import, SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP, two-module); freestanding cross-build audit: zero enum-discriminant-owner-unresolved warnings, only harmless rt_enum_new_none/enum_register_name fabrications (FsError has no None variant), strong rt_enum_new/id/discriminant/payload/check_variant symbols, identical 24-byte enum struct across runtime TUs, baked ids hash-match qualified names (FNV-1a enum_runtime_type_id). Root cause (historical): match arm tests baked the enum identity as an integer at HIR (module-local registry hash) while constructors qualified names later at MIR, so rt_enum_check_variant's id compare failed and matches fell through to zero; fix = requalify_enum_check_variant_ids + register_global_enums. Spec fserror_match_payload_native added (15-arm classifier + payload bindings, 7/7); pre-fix AOT binary kept for a cargo-capable Linux lane's RED replay. Residuals: the boot gate's current L4 failure (driver-open-failed) is a different open issue; pure-Simple twin was fixed at source (5deef7d3d5c). close_evidence reproducer=test/01_unit/compiler/native/fserror_match_payload_native_spec.spl prevention=test/01_unit/lib/fs_driver/nvfs_arena_sync_barrier_order_spec.spl"

